,0,396],[7096058,20390,5,0.369,0.259,[[10,74]],[["",44,0,1]],0,397],[7096005,20391,59,1.77,1.388,[[15,51]],[["",27,0,1],["",27,0,1],["",27,0,0],["",27,0,0]],0,398],[7105758,20392,1,0.116,0.083,[[18,26]],[],0,399],[7119738,20396,9,0.657,0.444,[[40,0.429,0,4],[41,0.357,0,4],[42,0.143,0,1],[43,0.071,0,0]],[],0,400],[7137878,20402,6,0.385,0.279,[[15,52]],[],0,400],[7137738,20402,6,0.385,0.279,[[15,53]],[["cc20b716_34db756f",27,0,1,"I think this is worth a comment: On non-Linux, and on expensive (ASan etc) bots, run only the single most important configuration, for capacity reasons."]],0,401],[7137284,20402,1,0.197,0.133,[[15,54]],[],0,402],[7100486,20403,83,3.042,2.433,[[15,0.943,55,79],[44,0.057,0,4]],[["",45,-11,1],["",45,-11,0],["7a242f14_4c469827",46,-8,1,"This should only be enabled if the mode is kSyncTransportOnly, right?"],["a01df061_d5f838b8",45,-8,1,"Do we still need this separately? Or would we want to migrate all callers to `AwaitSyncSetupCompletion`? (Definitely not as part of this CL, since there are lots of callers.) Also these two are…"],["0cb40422_22cf393e",28,-7,1,"Either in this patch or a follow-up, it would be great if this logic moves to a newly-introduced function in SyncServiceImplHarness, so the code here would look something like…"],["90b0a465_b68934fb",28,-7,1,"`SetSelectedTypes()` is somewhat deprecated, as with UNO we favor individual calls to `SetSelectedType()`. Would it be possible to use such function?"],["330b3457_d6889a73",46,-5,0,"Is this intentional? What it does is skip `SingleClientSharedTabGroupDataSyncTest::SetUp()`, which is kinda weird and very non-obvious. If it's intentional, please add a comment."],["dc963fa0_835c9bdb",47,-4,0,"Huh, this is kinda suspicious. Do you have any extra info about this? If this really can't be avoided, we should probably file a bug against the owners of this code."]],0,403],[7140380,20403,50,1.77,1.388,[[15,56]],[["ab020dfc_bed083be",45,0,0,"So this is the difference: We're now not checking `IsSyncFeatureActive` anymore. Most of what that does is redundant with other checks: E.g. we already CHECKed `IsInitialSyncFeatureSetupComplete` in…"]],0,404],[7141999,20403,32,1.77,1.388,[[15,57]],[["1cc0f6c2_bbd76a94",6,0,0,"That's pretty odd - any idea why we were only returning that for sync-the-feature before?"]],0,405],[7146299,20404,19,1.035,0.792,[[15,58]],[],0,406],[7146267,20404,51,1.77,1.388,[[15,59]],[["166059ad_738af8da",48,0,1,"I'm a bit surprised this was necessary - we shouldn't be running this test in transport mode on CrOS anyway, right?! Anyway, I think a better comment to add here is that signing out isn't supported…"]],0,407],[7150888,20405,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,60]],[],0,408],[7151123,20405,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,61]],[["a05c40d9_6ba3a1b5",49,0,0,"APPS and APP_SETTINGS are also effectively CrOS-only now, though I think we've never actually properly turned them off on WML - see crbug.com/40267153. So we could just scope the entire file to…"]],0,409],[7151099,20405,1,0.197,0.133,[[15,62]],[],0,410],[7151160,20405,10,0.597,0.431,[[15,63]],[["c83508c3_9ffe3a8b",50,0,1,"nit: This leaves one mental step to the reader (...and on ChromeOS, there's only Sync-the-feature)."]],0,411],[7150904,20405,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,64]],[],0,412],[7153640,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,65]],[],0,413],[7152765,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,66]],[],0,414],[7152764,20406,10,0.597,0.431,[[15,67]],[],0,415],[7152361,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,68]],[],0,416],[7153639,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,69]],[],0,417],[7152360,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,70]],[],0,418],[7151899,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,71]],[],0,419],[7152762,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,72]],[],0,420],[7152763,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,73]],[],0,421],[7152358,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,74]],[],0,422],[7152761,20406,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,75]],[],0,423],[7157643,20409,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,76]],[],0,424],[7156581,20410,14,0.597,0.431,[[15,77]],[],0,425],[7151999,20410,17,1.035,0.792,[[15,78]],[["a2af7359_e3c67627",6,-1,0,"I think we should create a bug (pretty sure a bug already exists for this) to fix this flakiness. Looks like it's stemming from autofill code. Skipping flakiness check is okay for this test since…"],["aeef0ee1_c0416739",51,-1,1,"nit, why not make the new element the last one in the tuple? That'd have avoided most of the changes in this file."]],0,426],[7166333,20410,8,0.597,0.431,[[15,79]],[["591f0046_2f263ab5",6,0,1,"Is that bug's title/description still accurate? Wouldn't SetupClientsAndSignIn() be the same as SetupSyncWithMode(SetupSyncMode::kSyncTransportOnly)?"],["cf263713_66a2e00f",6,0,1,"Could you add a bit more detail here? What's the goal of this CL specifically?"]],0,427],[7177303,20412,10,0.597,0.431,[[15,80]],[],0,428],[7204011,20420,5,0.385,0.279,[[15,81]],[],0,429],[7207187,20423,407,10.07,8.247,[[15,1.0,82,405]],[["0bb388f1_684c445c",52,-3,1,"Add the store param here too? (Or TODO for now)"],["262a6394_6da0545d",36,-3,1,"Since there's a few more instances of this below: Create a helper like `GetBookmarkSyncService()`?"],["41a4d7da_382cb2cf",36,-3,1,"Please specify the store here"],["4acbfaa0_51b1d53c",36,-3,0,"There's a bunch more fixture classes here that should also be addressed. Since this CL is large enough as it is, maybe keep them for a followup?"],["51eae9b8_5dd1d524",6,-3,1,"Was this to distinguish \"local\" as in \"local creation\" vs \"local store\"? FWIW, \"local creation\" is used fairly commonly (e.g. in `DataTypeEntityChange`), so if it's just that I'd stick with the old…"],["5db301c8_1aa8b1b8",36,-3,1,"Here maybe wait until the local creation makes it to the fakeserver? As it is, there's a race condition between the local creation and the remote creation. (Which probably doesn't really matter in…"],["67767ef7_a742c750",6,-3,0,"optional: Put this into a separate CL? There's some risk that the tests will be flaky on Android, and then the entire thing might get reverted."],["84d63c69_121258ff",36,-3,1,"Same here: Wait?"],["a0a52c5d_33c3d23f",36,-3,1,"`kSingleProfileIndex`?"],["e178d582_064eabb7",53,-3,1,"These should also be updated, but it can certainly be a separate CL. TODO for now?"],["fa124414_8167c9a9",36,-3,1,"Could you please undo the reordering? I do agree that the old order is weird and the new one is better, but doing this in the same CL as other changes makes reviewing very hard."]],0,430],[7205665,20423,66,3.042,2.433,[[15,83]],[["b2b9497a_3c8fae19",54,-3,0,"This makes sense, but I do wonder why it now became necessary. Can you explain?"]],0,431],[7224737,20426,24,1.035,0.792,[[15,84]],[],0,432],[7245859,20433,20,1.035,0.792,[[15,85]],[],0,433],[7210912,20433,36,1.77,1.388,[[15,86]],[["9e53c0f8_fbc21eb5",6,-10,1,"Any particular reason for removing this? I guess it's to make the parameterization simpler? It doesn't matter *much* but usually you'd leave the feature override in as long as the feature itself…"],["c215d31b_a285ea53",55,0,1,"nit: This name seems a bit weird; I can't quite parse it? Maybe just `UsePrimaryIcon()`?"]],0,434],[7252072,20433,28,1.035,0.792,[[15,87]],[],0,435],[7252710,20433,32,1.77,1.388,[[15,88]],[],0,436]]}